 stem:"An 80-year-old man with a history of chronic kidney disease came to the emergency room with dyspnea for 1 day. He denied chest pain. He took ibuprofen for hip pain during the past 7 days. PE: pitting edema of both legs. Lungs: fine crackles at both lower lungs. The ECG is shown in the figure. What is the most likely diagnosis?",
 gray:"A 80-year-old man with history of chronic kidney disease came to emergency room with dyspnea for 1 day. He denied chest pain. He took ibuprofen for hip pain during the past 7 days. PE: pitting edema both legs Lung: fine crackles both lower lungs ECG as figure. What is the most likely diagnosis? — 1. Hypercalcemia 2. Early repolarization 3. Acute pericarditis 4. Hyperkalemia 5. Acute myocardial infarction",
 opts:["Hypercalcemia","Early repolarization","Acute pericarditis","Hyperkalemia","Acute myocardial infarction"],ans:3,key:"D Hyperkalemia"+KS,
 opinion:"เห็นด้วยกับคีย์ มั่นใจสูง: CKD + NSAID ทำให้ GFR ลดและ hyporeninemic hypoaldosteronism → K สูง ECG มี tall peaked T wave ชัดใน precordial leads",
 notes:"ผู้จดไฮไลต์ฟ้าที่ T wave สูงแหลมใน V3 (ลบออกจากรูปโจทย์แล้ว) · แปะสไลด์ 18. Lecture_413 basic ECG interpretation ข้างช้อย: ECG severe hyperkalemia — T wave สูงมาก, QRS กว้าง, P wave หาย · ใต้ข้อแปะสไลด์ ECG ของช้อยอื่นพร้อมเลขกำกับ: Hypercalcemia — short QT · Hypokalemia — flat T wave, prominent U wave, ST depression · WPW syndrome → preexcitation · S1Q3T3 pattern acute pulmonary embolism → PE · Acute pericarditis — diffuse ST elevation concave upward, PR depression",
 guide:"KDIGO 2024 CKD Guideline; Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine 22e (2025) — Hyperkalemia",
